{"id":"075ad11d-7fd0-49e3-b744-f31aad6f6c64","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ec2fd80021679e63","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1ed44a8b459ed0f94ed30cb71fd5a001668fa95f","start":5027,"end":5071},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","capabilityLines","\"",":","Map","<","string",",","Set","<","number",">",">",";"]},"context":{"before":"5841403d9c651163","after":"627a613ffa82e3bf"}},"payload":{"text":"1-based lines pre-armed as capability breakpoints (policy said stop), by program file — so a stop there reports\nreason \"capability\" rather than \"breakpoint\". The entry's computed at launch from the policy the adapter sent;\nanother file's as it loads (noteProgramFile).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:33.367Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:33.367Z"}
{"id":"08c3d983-ef28-4c0a-a9e0-34635194bab4","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"52861c7ef0e156ee","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"3895bfec34c1ee21272d4c0584a3bff4b140bc9a","start":10166,"end":10218},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","guestProcess","\"",":","{","\"","exitCode","\"","?",":","number","}","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"ffb8685108392002","after":"76ff3fc81b5df721"}},"payload":{"text":"The program's `process`, for the exit code it sets (`process.exitCode`) when it finishes on its own.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:48.161Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:48.161Z"}
{"id":"0a1f1696-8072-4319-a5a8-fc155731e765","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2da95c8a18fd27d9","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"63707e308100484114e02f47e67bcf6d9bc1b690","start":10816,"end":10870},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","programFsFor","\"",":","(","(","cwd",":","string",")","=>","FsShim",")","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"76ff3fc81b5df721","after":"573bcb6ac25ef2bb"}},"payload":{"text":"The program's own `fs` for a run in `cwd`: almostnode's over the editor's runtime files (runtime-vfs.ts) — each of\nits calls on a workspace file the editor's to decide, make and keep among the run's effects, as any debugger's\nprogram's are. Undefined outside the editor (no runtime link): the program's `fs` is then the runtime's own.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:44.375Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:44.375Z"}
{"id":"13067314-7b5b-47ca-ba37-47f621cdaf36","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f1d224dab132004e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8fb0a7692d9c53e2e69d3ecce52208602296a876","start":1473,"end":2251},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","countLinkCalls","(","link",":","RuntimeConnection",")",":","RuntimeConnection","{","const","counted","=","<","T","extends","(","...","args",":","never","[]",")","=>","unknown",">","(","what",":","string",",","call",":","T",")",":","T","=>","(","(","...","args",":","Parameters","<","T",">",")","=>","{","const","started","=","performance",".","now","(",")",";","const","tally","=","linkCalls",".","get","(","what",")","??","{","\"","calls","\"",":","0",",","\"","ms","\"",":","0",",","\"","failed","\"",":","0","}",";","linkCalls",".","set","(","what",",","tally",")",";","tally",".","calls","+=","1",";","try","{","return","call","(","...","args",")",";","}","catch","(","error",")","{","tally",".","failed","+=","1",";","throw","error",";","}","finally","{","tally",".","ms","+=","performance",".","now","(",")","-","started",";","}","}",")","as","T",";","for","(","const","[","name",",","call","]","of","Object",".","entries","(","link",".","fs",")",")","{","(","link",".","fs","as","unknown","as","Record","<","string",",","unknown",">",")","[","name","]","=","counted","(","name",",","call",")",";","}","link",".","tarball","=","counted","(","\"","tarball","\"",",","link",".","tarball",")",";","link",".","decide","=","counted","(","\"","decide","\"",",","link",".","decide",")",";","return","link",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"fa5739cca6d5f015","after":"2f06a481c43ea00c"}},"payload":{"text":"`link`, each call it makes of the editor counted: a run's file calls, a package's tarball, a package's call decided\nthere — each a blocking round trip, thousands a run, so counted rather than spanned (CLAUDE.md, *Spans*: hot paths),\nand told on the run's span as it ends (linkCallsSince). The editor counts the same calls as it answers them (the\nmetrics plane's `runtime-fs`); these are the run's, and the time the run waited.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:50.044Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:50.044Z"}
{"id":"145f7516-31fe-4562-a125-ea8e516cd50b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"392fe78925fbbe2b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e9af984b09727786ac16c5fe330fa77f98827e94","start":7952,"end":8006},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","awaitAction","\"",":","(","(","action",":","Action",")","=>","void",")","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"520f43881439d7d1","after":"3e9495e0ef31b072"}},"payload":{"text":"Resolver for the control message the session loop is currently awaiting (top-level, async pause).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:03.450Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:03.450Z"}
{"id":"1da8e29b-1f5b-4bbd-a81c-feb3af3cb205","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"76ff3fc81b5df721","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"5cd88b3a00f602ac036c46627ab08b097e131d85","start":10329,"end":10360},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","runtime","\"",":","Runtime","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"52861c7ef0e156ee","after":"2da95c8a18fd27d9"}},"payload":{"text":"The program's module system (packages/tsval/README.md, *Modules*): almostnode on the shared workspace — resolution, the module graph, the\ncache — with tsval evaluating the program's own files (programModules). A package's built-ins are almostnode's, its\nwrites refused (a library's effects aren't stepped or asked about); the program's are its stand-ins (programBuiltins:\nwhat a capability stop is about). Loaded at a run's start.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:46.240Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:46.240Z"}
{"id":"1fc7fb39-ac90-40c2-9a30-e51df705a4a8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3e9495e0ef31b072","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"899211fa7d5ed8fdd8ec08984270915757c0ef2d","start":8114,"end":8154},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","actionTrace","\"",":","TraceContext","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"392fe78925fbbe2b","after":"1f1ace92ca41e0c7"}},"payload":{"text":"Trace context of the control message currently being handled — so the step span it drives continues the\nadapter's trace (one cross-context trace per debug action). Set just before the awaited action resolves.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:01.665Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:01.665Z"}
{"id":"220ac30d-6116-40c4-8bc4-13f93d93786d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"4899b60c5dec573b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"53992e549cdcc5a941f96ecf95a8348bd4ca1012","start":7200,"end":7220},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","skipNext","\"",":","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"b87c6e3b32bd2ca5","after":"b4d95134e6efc515"}},"payload":{"text":"The call at the capability stop the user skipped (RUNTIME-EVIDENCE.md, *Capability decisions, on the line*): it isn't made, the run goes on with its inert\nstand-in's result.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:10.906Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:10.906Z"}
{"id":"226159d5-8ece-4d19-893e-f59ad7793d71","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"d0e5ee2712aff789","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"816e98c2bda98d1d140b1c797b300431375caaa9","start":8914,"end":8940},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","current","\"",":","Vm","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"1f1ace92ca41e0c7","after":"844bc984fd56bdec"}},"payload":{"text":"The VM on the timeline being shown — what coverage reports on. A forward step advances a fork; a step back\nreturns to an earlier stop.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:57.817Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:57.817Z"}
{"id":"229a5dca-af35-4bda-8bcc-1344d59e01c8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"540cdc1907044e3c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"28c8b8949a229112f3ba92b606462b1b6b6e0f0d","start":13450,"end":13472},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","testsFailed","\"",":","number",";"]},"context":{"before":"799f9c1429c96005","after":"da6f3e315031cd97"}},"payload":{"text":"How many tests failed, as node-test.js tells at the end: a run with one fails, as `node --test` does.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:25.172Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:25.172Z"}
{"id":"264f32af-b58a-4fa9-9eb7-24c2b761c18b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2f06a481c43ea00c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"5d5bd54429c93f8c286da99800ec1d51db72e961","start":2700,"end":2996},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","linkCallsSince","(",")",":","Record","<","string",",","number",">","{","const","told","=","Object",".","fromEntries","(","[","...","linkCalls","]",".","flatMap","(","(","[","what",",","{","calls",",","ms",",","failed","}","]",")","=>","[","[","what",",","calls","]",",","[","what","+","\"","Ms","\"",",","Math",".","round","(","ms",")","]",",","...","failed",">","0","?","[","[","what","+","\"","Failed","\"",",","failed","]","]",":","[","]","]",")",")",";","linkCalls",".","clear","(",")",";","return","told",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"f1d224dab132004e","after":"6ccf4735cf31b840"}},"payload":{"text":"The calls counted since the last asking, as a span's attributes — `stat: 8750, statMs: 4700, statFailed: 12` — and\nthe count started again.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:48.088Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:48.088Z"}
{"id":"2cf8e8d3-4e38-450f-bdf1-515036e66fff","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8ee50ac3d4556234","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"63d9766013546c75348d43ff29cfce49e7878a24","start":6805,"end":6850},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","giveNext","\"",":","{","\"","value","\"",":","unknown","}","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"302e3511bd3492db","after":"b87c6e3b32bd2ca5"}},"payload":{"text":"The result the user gave the call at a capability stop, once (`decide` with `give`): the next stand-in call returns it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:14.578Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:14.578Z"}
{"id":"315f6030-430f-4a4d-8f0f-616bb6893731","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2254c00895e2bbad","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"de55796c9d4f5e2f1747ba3c3701f7411b5f9df7","start":7820,"end":7836},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","history","\"",":","Vm","[]",";"]},"context":{"before":"27d260224ce755eb","after":"7783130bc694b373"}},"payload":{"text":"Forks, one per stop reached; `index` is the currently-displayed stop.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:05.364Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:05.364Z"}
{"id":"3415117e-3602-4cf9-a299-410e7081da92","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2433f854b041bb00","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"398376d760a66c79f7ebc0c9a18cd9fce8c1e10a","start":11393,"end":11428},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","runGlobal","\"",":","RunGlobal","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"573bcb6ac25ef2bb","after":"9a31782c957d7e4e"}},"payload":{"text":"The run's own global, as a Node process has one (almostnode's run-global.ts): its packages' `globalThis`, and the\nprogram's names that only they set (sharedGlobals) — so what a package does to its globals (just-bash's sandbox\nputs Proxies over `performance` and the timers) is the run's, not this worker's, whose are the debugger's.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:40.522Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:40.522Z"}
{"id":"346beeed-b442-40d7-a134-cd045cb49296","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2cc8f096ba3f8796","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8724e99829173c8d21983d99865a18a2df448fd7","start":12818,"end":12849},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","pins","\"",":","Record","<","string",",","string",">",";"]},"context":{"before":"2072780367e94654","after":"bad44f61f9adcbbd"}},"payload":{"text":"The version the editor pins of each package (`.silo/versions.json`, read as a run starts): what's installed.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:30.967Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:30.967Z"}
{"id":"43a69ee2-fbd2-42e8-950b-f41ce7796c3e","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"302e3511bd3492db","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c8b269f641ecad98125fd8ce1f7b2ec4d1a9d83c","start":6670,"end":6690},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","denyNext","\"",":","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"fd9248dbdaf949e7","after":"8ee50ac3d4556234"}},"payload":{"text":"\"Deny\" at a capability stop: the next capability call fails, as a denied one would. Reset at every stop.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:16.607Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:16.607Z"}
{"id":"466256f5-e18b-4476-a6a8-c5543cc07c3c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"cf0b1582be5af834","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"44ce7a0bd9332c839c61bb6640d0056ac88415c3","start":12081,"end":12152},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","packageDirOf","\"",":","(","(","filename",":","string",")","=>","string","|","undefined",")","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"ed91e7118918084b","after":"2072780367e94654"}},"payload":{"text":"almostnode's `packageDirOf`, once the runtime's loaded.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:34.764Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:34.764Z"}
{"id":"49d75bb3-ee9b-4efd-a1d8-9c75c9c2ddbe","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"799f9c1429c96005","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"4f841548a0306cb4143eb467fe3102f40e4e8868","start":13091,"end":13126},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","windowReach","\"",":","TestReport","[","\"","files","\"","]",";"]},"context":{"before":"bad44f61f9adcbbd","after":"540cdc1907044e3c"}},"payload":{"text":"What the window a test's page drove ran, told as the page let it go (the shell's, `playwright.run`'s `release`, with\nthe dev server instrumented): the code of the editor in it, in every realm of it. The test ending next takes it as\nits own (its page is let go by an `after` of its, just before it ends).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:27.112Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:27.112Z"}
{"id":"4fec90bb-7c32-43eb-b5e7-da80cbeb1c3b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f0003962631e93fb","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c7592611b28f61618692e16c631981e114fbec3d","start":5544,"end":5587},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","programFiles","\"",":","Map","<","string",",","ts",".","SourceFile",">",";"]},"context":{"before":"627a613ffa82e3bf","after":"f65eafedc411bfbf"}},"payload":{"text":"The program's files known so far — the entry, and each other one as it loads — parsed for their capability calls.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:29.617Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:29.617Z"}
{"id":"58756164-a828-4786-bd2d-9d4da97dc585","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8ba5ee0ddc57c828","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"4e01060639a335a2249ae49f7d796d1ab49c2d79","start":3809,"end":3866},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","Place","{","\"","file","\"",":","string",";","\"","line","\"",":","number","}"]},"context":{"before":"08c6c08f4dbf4249","after":"b8ff55fcd0f84fd6"}},"payload":{"text":"Where the run is: a program file and a 1-based line in it — the entry's, or another of the program's (packages/tsval/README.md, *Modules*).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:42.591Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:42.591Z"}
{"id":"5c0bf73b-0fc5-4964-91f1-ecb0b6f03db3","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b87c6e3b32bd2ca5","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d2513d36174c8aafd49b76189a97a650dda66fed","start":6980,"end":7001},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","allowNext","\"",":","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"8ee50ac3d4556234","after":"4899b60c5dec573b"}},"payload":{"text":"\"Allow once\" (or this run, or always) at a capability stop: the next capability call the policy doesn't allow happens\nfor real all the same — the one asked about. Reset at every stop.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:12.709Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:12.709Z"}
{"id":"612fff3e-3022-4509-a888-26d807190395","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"bae040e4df79fe8d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"955c0e93ca9aa0be67f787a5587b5919122daa47","start":6106,"end":6157},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","runLayer","\"",":","ReturnType","<","typeof","layered",">","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"9a2710229c343d0e","after":"16ed512890ee7dc8"}},"payload":{"text":"A live run's own writable layer over the workspace's files: its writes go there and are gone when it ends.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:24.038Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:24.038Z"}
{"id":"63e84097-c4c7-4ecd-b96a-4986e243c38c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"da6f3e315031cd97","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b13588dc1c8e41dd11cbef446c9926d7a16ed451","start":13584,"end":13605},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","testsDone","\"",":","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"540cdc1907044e3c","after":"f28ddf5220552420"}},"payload":{"text":"Whether node-test.js has told that the file's tests are all done: past it, only what Node counts as keeping a process\nalive keeps the run going (advanceFrom).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:23.174Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:23.174Z"}
{"id":"695ed80d-843e-41bf-afed-d2023da6ea30","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2072780367e94654","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a7d7f84624d21bf178b3d5ea56fa3728b4e4f0fa","start":12218,"end":12317},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","baseline","\"",":","{","\"","consumer","\"","?",":","Record","<","string",",","WsConsumer",">",";","\"","packages","\"","?",":","BaselinePackages","}","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"cf0b1582be5af834","after":"2cc8f096ba3f8796"}},"payload":{"text":"The dependency baseline (`.silo/baseline.json`, read as a run starts): what the part of each package the code uses\ncould reach when it began to (the join, its `consumer`), and what each package's own code could do when the library\nwas added (its `packages`) — what grew since isn't settled: it asks, unless the policy allows it. Undefined when\nthere's none (the editor makes it as a project opens, unless `silo.baseline` is off): the policy decides every\npackage's call.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:32.907Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:32.907Z"}
{"id":"6aeb6e21-1c26-40c9-b515-28fd75221123","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"844bc984fd56bdec","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a4fb0d578d712873ef6704cd812264f441ffaa25","start":9090,"end":9122},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","sumsOf","\"",":","WeakMap","<","Vm",",","SiteSums",">",";"]},"context":{"before":"d0e5ee2712aff789","after":"f3ef6db1eb8f2c71"}},"payload":{"text":"What went through each observed site on each timeline (tsval's `observe`), and the sums being added to now, the\ntimeline running's: a fork starts from a copy of its stop's, as its coverage starts from a copy of its counts.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:55.939Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:55.939Z"}
{"id":"7cd3d375-d0c3-44a1-bc5d-86d5d682bd39","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"08c6c08f4dbf4249","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"59a93a2f36292238f6401f4c1fa51743359786ec","start":3655,"end":3741},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","post","(","message",":","WorkerEvent",")",":","void","{","globalThis",".","postMessage","(","message",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"c91a11e124210adf","after":"8ba5ee0ddc57c828"}},"payload":{"text":"An event for the adapter, on this session's event subject.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:44.414Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:44.414Z"}
