{"id":"f2eb96de-a2d9-4947-8cbe-cfc3691969de","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1f1ace92ca41e0c7","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9825108a635ddf514c6fda8fab16c50fde4b823b","start":8378,"end":8412},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","control","\"",":","Int32Array","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"3e9495e0ef31b072","after":"d0e5ee2712aff789"}},"payload":{"text":"Shared control word for the SYNCHRONOUS in-handler pause. A breakpoint reached inside a host-invoked guest call\n(a server's request handler, a library's callback, a program file a package requires) can't pause by awaiting — the call is on a synchronous stack the worker\nloop doesn't drive — so the onBreakpoint hook blocks the whole worker on `Atomics.wait` while the main\nthread stays live, and the adapter resumes it via `Atomics.notify`. control[0]: 0 = waiting, 1 = go.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:59.741Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:59.741Z"}
